> use a standard SCSI drive.  Is this possible?  I also found in the
> install docs the partition table setup for each of the recommended RZ
> drives.   Will I have to replicate this partitioning on my OTS drive?
> There are overlaid partitions on the RZs.  How do I do this?  Is there a
> disk partitioning tool available from the SRM?   Can I use the SRM to
> wipe out the partition tables on the new drive.   I've installed other
> Unix's and they all have some tool for patitioning the disk as the OS
> needs it.  Is this available in the DU install?

A while ago, it was noted that with respect to using third-party disks
with DU or OVMS, you could run into problems.

To make a long story short, DEC blamed Seagate's firmware, and Seagate
blamed DEC for making their operating system specifically reject
non-DEC-branded drives (DEC branded drives are usually just Seagate
Barracudas anyways..).

I would suggest that if you are able to, buy a SCSI drive and try it out
on the Alphastation.  If you can't get it to work, then put the SCSI
drive onto a PeeCee somewhere and get a DEC/Compaq branded RZ disk
(uugh..  Compaq RZ..  ick..).  Unfortunatly, you will pay significantly
more.

The newer versions of DEC Unix are said to be not as sensitive though,
as are the newer versions of OVMS.  But it certainly was a problem in
the 5.5-2 era of OVMS, and 2.0 of DEC Unix (or OSF/1 -- I forget the
exact timetable when they changed the name, and Compaq has announced
they've come up with yet another name for it..).



