Hi,

A couple of year back I remember seeing someone using EMACS on OpenVMS
with a key mapping done by an init file that allowed the standard EDT
style keystrokes to be used for editing, eg PF4 and Gold-PF4 to remove
and then replace the line.

Does anyone know where I can get such an init file so that EMACS on
Digital UNIX will allow me to use the same, or do I have to roll my own
?

If there is such an init file I think this should go in the FAQ

At the moment I am switching between EMACS on Unix, ED/TPU on OpenVMS
and the usual WinTel editors with CTR-C and CTR-V for cust and paste....

I know, I know "why not use EMACS everywhere", but I do not have the
disk space right now to do this.

Any pointers appreciated.

Regards
