Hi again,

Found the following which work fine for me....
from:

http://www.ornl.gov/its/archives/mailing-lists/alpha-osf-managers/1997/04/msg00221.html

Regards
John Cushnie
cushnie@csi.com

==========================================================


Cut and paste this into the .emacs file in your home directory.

;; file .emacs
( tpu-edt )
;;;
(setq default-major-mode 'text-mode)
(setq text-mode-hook 'turn-on-auto-fill)
(setq-default fill-column 78)
(setq-default line-number-mode)
;;;
;; Control-s and Control-q are used for flow control (Xon/Xoff flow
control).
;; Disable emacs' use of these characters.
(global-unset-key "\C-s")
(global-unset-key "\C-q")

Then startup emacs and follow the instructions to map your keyboard....

And then the keypad command work....

Bit tricky to set up with the PC keyboard though..... missing keys on the
keypad...






